    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are leaning heavily on **Gunnar Henderson** today as our premier start, with an efficiency score of 62.18. Despite facing a formidable arm in Woo (xERA 3.48), **Gunnar Henderson** gains significant leverage from his batting order (#2) and a favorable platoon dynamic, providing the highest ceiling among today\u2019s starters. We are also monitoring **Miguel Vargas** closely (57.90); while his matchup against Weathers is standard, the combination of a favorable wind and the opposing pitcher's slow delivery creates an ideal environment for him to exploit the stolen base category, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.38) and **Jacob Wilson** (60.70) round out a stable core, though both carry the risks associated with \"Lineup Pending\" status.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on **Josh Jung**, whose 42.87 efficiency score landed him on the bench in favor of **Brayan Rocchio** (41.40) and **Nolan Schanuel** (56.87). While **Josh Jung** is a viable talent, the optimizer penalized him for a difficult matchup against Ryan, viewing the potential for empty plate appearances as too costly against our game cap constraints. Meanwhile, **Wade Meckler** remains a cautionary case; he provided a score of 37.47, but his likely position at the bottom of the order and a challenging L/L platoon matchup against Gage Jump make him a non-starter for today. We continue to hold **Kyle Tucker** and **Jackson Merrill** in reserve, as they are not scheduled for play today, leaving us to rely on our active core to navigate these matchups without the benefit of our full roster strength.",
